# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════
#  Transformer Asset Map — Environment Config
# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════
#  Copy this file to .env and fill in the values.
#  Never commit .env to Git — it is in .gitignore.
# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════

# ── Option A: Supabase Cloud (default) ────────────
# Get these from: https://supabase.com/dashboard/project/_/settings/api
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project-id.supabase.co
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=your-anon-public-key-here

# ── Security cutover: Supabase Auth ───────────────
# Set to 1 to authenticate through Supabase Auth so the database RLS (keyed to
# auth.uid()) actually enforces per-user access. REQUIRES the hardening
# migration (20261121000001) and scripts/link-supabase-auth-users.mjs to have
# been applied first — see MIGRATION_SUPABASE_AUTH.md. Leave unset/0 to use the
# legacy login until you are ready to cut over.
# VITE_USE_SUPABASE_AUTH=0
# Synthetic-email domain for username-based login (must match the script's
# AUTH_EMAIL_DOMAIN). Any non-routable domain is fine.
# VITE_AUTH_EMAIL_DOMAIN=asset.local

# ── Option B: Supabase Local Docker ───────────────
# After running `npm run db:start`, run `npm run db:status` to get the anon key.
# VITE_SUPABASE_URL=http://localhost:54321
# VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=<anon key from `supabase status` output>

# ── 3D Globe view (Cesium) — optional ─────────────
# Both keys can also be entered inside the app (3D View → API keys), where they
# are saved in the browser only. Values here act as the default for everyone.
# Cesium ion (free): https://ion.cesium.com/tokens — unlocks 3D buildings,
# world terrain and Bing aerial imagery.
# VITE_CESIUM_ION_TOKEN=
# Google Maps Platform key with the "Map Tiles API" enabled — unlocks Google
# Photorealistic 3D Tiles.
# VITE_GOOGLE_MAPS_API_KEY=
